; The mixed bignum-times-inexact route of the integer-division trio, where the
; divisor is an inexact zero. R7RS 6.2.6 makes it an error; this route was the
; one place that answered +nan.0 instead of raising, so a bignum computation
; that hit a zero divisor produced a number and carried on.
;
; `/` is deliberately NOT part of this: an inexact zero divisor there is
; ordinary IEEE-754 division, gated by corpus/52_bignum_inexact_zero_division.esk.
(display (modulo (expt 2 100) 0.0))
(display "MUST-NOT-PRINT")
